## Delivered

Frozen contract: src/ClientIntake/ with 51 exported types across Models,
Contracts, and Services. Every workflow constructor and method throws
NotImplementedException; the module implements none of its own ports; nothing in
the portal references, registers, resolves, or invokes it. IIntakeStore has
exactly two firm-omitting members, both keyed-digest lookups returning trusted
scope. IIntakeContentStore exposes no read member.

Blazor foundation: App, Routes, PortalLayout, ReviewPage. No component declares
@rendermode or @page; no global render mode is applied; static SSR is the
default. ReviewEndpoints.cs returns RazorComponentResult<ReviewPage> with one
closed ReviewPageModel, and retains its route, policy, headers, trusted-firm
extraction, browser-safety guard, closed projection, invariant amounts,
collection order, single FindAsync call with the request cancellation token, and
identical empty 404.

## Two defects found and avoided

1. MapStaticAssets() registers a {**path:file} catch-all over the whole URL
   space. It turned GET /sign-out from 405 into 404 and added an endpoint in the
   "neither anonymous nor authorization-required" third state spec 011 forbids.
   Replaced with UseStaticFiles() middleware, which adds no endpoint.
2. A [property: JsonIgnore] target on a positional parameter whose property is
   declared by hand is discarded by the compiler (CS0657) while looking exactly
   like a working omission. It had left two Fingerprint properties serializable.

## AC-99 storage neutrality — verified against master

git diff --name-only master shows no file under src/Persistence, src/Tenancy,
src/TaxCases, src/CaseReview, src/CaseProcessing, src/DocumentExtraction, or
src/TaxLogicEngine; no EF migration; no model snapshot; no schema artifact; no
persisted or review public contract.

## Scope exceptions — two files outside T01's owned list

1. tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Upgrade/DotNet10RepositoryTests.cs
   Spec 013 shipped a closed-set assertion over every project in TaxAI.sln,
   which the root CLAUDE.md forbids. It blocked this task's required solution
   additions outright. Replaced with per-project presence-and-uniqueness; the two
   ClientIntake paths added to ApprovedProjects; every other assertion in the
   file untouched. EXPLICITLY AUTHORIZED BY THE HUMAN before implementation
   began, after the blocker was reported with options.

2. scripts/Assert-DotNet10Toolchain.ps1
   The same defect in the executable preflight. Fixed additively: the two
   ClientIntake paths were added to the $approvedProjects registry. No assertion
   weakened; the set stays closed and still rejects any unregistered project.
   Discovered only when the gate ran, after the authorization above.

Both are recorded in PR #133 for the reviewer.

## Amended assertions (T01 requirement 13)

Replaced with tighter exact allowlists, never deleted or broadly weakened:
portal public-type set, host route inventory, two production-file lists,
per-file registration tokens, additive baseline signatures, the route/auth
additive endpoint set, and the static-file surface. New component scans added for
AC-90/91/96/98, which the .cs-only scanners could not see. Both superseded rows
are registered in AmendmentAuditTests against the immutable spec 012 PRD ledger.

## Deliberately not shipped

No intake route, workflow body, relational intake table, or encrypted content
adapter. No interactive component. Interactive Server is registered per T01
requirement 5 and the approved architecture, adding the framework's five
/_blazor and /_framework/opaque-redirect endpoints; no component opts in, so the
circuit has no component to run and no taxpayer model to carry. Flagged in the
PR as something a reviewer may reasonably want deferred to T03.

Deployment refusal unchanged: Development-only startup, and no deployment
anywhere that can receive real taxpayer data.

